| **Can I visit the monastery on the same day as the Belém Tower?** | Yes – the combined ticket covers both and you can enter each site at any time on the same day. |
| **Is there a discount for children or seniors?** | Children (under 12) enter free when accompanied by a paying adult; seniors (65 +) receive a €2 discount on the general admission. |
| **Do I need a reservation for the interior of the church?** | No – the church is open to all ticket‑holders, but guided tours require a reservation. |
| **Is there a “skip‑the‑line” option?** | Some third‑party vendors (e.g., Viator) sell a “fast‑track” ticket that lets you bypass the regular queue. |
| **What’s the best time to visit to avoid crowds?** | Early morning (right at opening) or late afternoon (after 16:00) are usually less crowded. |

